 task information\\n- Update Mechanism: Manages real-time synchronization\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Languages and Frameworks\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n  - Rationale: Strong typing, excellent file/JSON parsing, cross-platform compatibility\\n  - Alternatives Considered: Bash scripting (too limited), Node.js (unnecessary complexity)\\n\\n### Key Libraries\\n- `json`: Native JSON parsing\\n- `rich`: Advanced terminal formatting and color support\\n- `watchdog`: File system monitoring for real-time updates\\n- `colorama`: Cross-platform terminal color support\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Task Parser (`task_parser.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Read project tracking JSON from `~/.ensemble/projects/`\\n- Parse and validate task metadata\\n- Extract task status, progress, and details\\n\\n**Input**: Project JSON file\\n**Output**: Structured task data\\n\\n### 2. Display Formatter (`display_manager.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Convert parsed tasks to human-readable format\\n- Apply color coding and status icons\\n- Generate task summary statistics\\n\\n**Features**:\\n- Status icon mapping: \\n  - \\u2705 Completed tasks\\n  - \\u26a1 In-progress tasks\\n  - \\u23f3 Pending tasks\\n  - \\u274c Blocked tasks\\n\\n### 3. Update Watcher (`file_watcher.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Monitor project tracking file for changes\\n- Trigger task list refresh\\n- Handle file access errors gracefully\\n\\n## D. Data Flow Diagram\\n```\\n[Project JSON] \\u2192 [Task Parser] \\u2192 [Validation] \\u2192 [Display Formatter] \\u2192 [Terminal Display]\\n                      \\u2191                               \\u2193\\n               [File Watcher] \\u2190----------- [Periodic Refresh]\\n```\\n\\n## E. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\ntmux_monitoring_dashboard/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 scripts/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 monitoring/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_watcher.py        # Main script\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_parser.py          # JSON parsing logic\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 display_manager.py      # Formatting and display\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 file_watcher.py         # Real-time update mechanism\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 requirements.txt                # Python dependencies\\n```\\n\\n## F. Error Handling Strategy\\n- Graceful handling of missing/malformed project files\\n- Configurable logging for debugging\\n- Fallback display for incomplete data\\n- Retry mechanisms for file access issues\\n\\n## G. Performance Considerations\\n- Lightweight parsing (minimal CPU usage)\\n- Efficient file watching\\n- Update interval: 1-2 seconds\\n- Minimal memory footprint\\n\\n## H. Deployment Approach\\n- Callable as standalone Python script\\n- Embeddable in tmux dashboard\\n- Cross-platform compatibility (macOS, Linux)\\n\\n## I. Testing Strategy\\n1. Unit Tests\\n   - Task parsing accuracy\\n   - Display formatting\\n   - Error handling scenarios\\n\\n2. Integration Tests\\n   - File watching reliability\\n   - Real-time update performance\\n   - Tmux integration\\n\\n## J. Open Questions / User Input Needed\\n- Preferred update interval (currently 1-2 seconds)\\n- Desired level of task detail in display\\n- Custom color scheme preferences\\n\\n## K. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Risk**: Inconsistent project file format\\n   **Mitigation**: Robust schema validation, default values\\n\\n2. **Risk**: Performance overhead\\n   **Mitigation**: Efficient parsing, minimal background processing\\n\\n3. **Risk**: Cross-platform compatibility\\n   **Mitigation**: Extensive testing, use of cross-platform libraries"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015Xpsvut8b8QEYESFmjJ83H', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Backend Tasks', 'description': 'Backend implementation for real-time monitoring system with file watching and task updates'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015Xpsvut8b8QEYESFmjJ83H', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "57ff1b63", "message": "Created project: Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Backend Tasks", "summary": {"project_id": "57ff1b63", "project_name": "Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Backend Tasks", "description": "Backend implementation for real-time monitoring system with file watching and task updates", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T23:05:16.452643", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T23:05:16.452643", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T23:05:16.452643", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Backend Tasks\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WfwacG2VTqGCF7bjqDMzTD', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m2.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Tmux Monitoring Dashboard\n\n## Core Task Breakdown\n\n### 1. Task Parser Implementation\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Description**: Develop robust JSON parsing mechanism for project tracking files\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Parses JSON files from `~/.ensemble/projects/`\n- Validates task schema \n- Handles missing/malformed data gracefully\n- Extracts key task metadata (status, progress, details)\n\n**Dependencies**: \n- File access permissions\n- Project tracking JSON schema\n\n### 2. File Watching Mechanism\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Description**: Implement real-time file monitoring for project tracking updates\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Uses `watchdog` library for file system events\n- Detects changes in project tracking JSON\n- Triggers task list refresh with minimal delay\n- Configurable update interval (1-2 seconds)\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- Task Parser implementation\n- Error handling strategy\n\n### 3. Display Data Preparation\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Description**: Transform parsed task data into display-ready format\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Converts task metadata to structured display data\n- Applies color coding and status icons\n- Generates task summary statistics\n- Supports multiple task statuses (completed, in-progress, pending, blocked)\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- Task Parser implementation\n- Color scheme configuration\n\n### 4. Error Handling & Logging\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Description**: Implement robust error management for file access and parsing\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Graceful handling of file read errors\n- Configurable logging mechanism\n- Fallback display for incomplete data\n- Retry strategies for transient file access issues\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- File Watching Mechanism\n- Task Parser implementation\n\n### 5. Performance Optimization\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Description**: Ensure lightweight and efficient task monitoring\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Minimal CPU usage during parsing\n- Low memory footprint\n- Fast update cycle (1-2 seconds)\n- Efficient file watching implementation\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- All previous task implementations\n\n## Testing Requirements\n1. Unit Tests to Validate:\n- Task parsing accuracy\n- File watching reliability\n- Display formatting logic\n- Error handling scenarios\n\n2. Integration Tests to Verify:\n- Real-time update performance\n- Cross-platform compatibility\n- Tmux dashboard integration\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n- Inconsistent project file formats: Implement robust schema validation\n- Performance overhead: Use efficient parsing techniques\n- Cross-platform compatibility: Extensive testing with cross-platform libraries\n\n## Technology Stack\n- Language: Python 3.9+\n- Key Libraries: \n  - `json` for parsing\n  - `rich` for terminal formatting\n  - `watchdog` for file monitoring\n  - `colorama` for color support'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WfwacG2VTqGCF7bjqDMzTD', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m2.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m2_20260116_230531.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m2_20260116_230531.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns,