{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 23:06:37", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-4c3c341a-cc8a-47a6-b2f2-bf6d08a70851', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Implement a real-time monitoring system for the Tmux Monitoring Dashboard that watches project tracking JSON files and provides live task status updates with rich terminal formatting",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard",\n  "test_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/tests",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/architecture_m2.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LoRMpMeiaHk5kbj6pYEMoF', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/architecture_m2.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LoRMpMeiaHk5kbj6pYEMoF', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Milestone 2 Architecture\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Purpose\\nDevelop an intelligent task monitoring system that provides real-time, visually intuitive tracking of agent tasks within the ensemble project management workflow.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\nAdopted a modular, event-driven design with separation of concerns:\\n- Data Parsing Layer: Responsible for reading and interpreting project state\\n- Display Layer: Handles formatting and rendering of task information\\n- Update Mechanism: Manages real-time synchronization\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Languages and Frameworks\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n  - Rationale: Strong typing, excellent file/JSON parsing, cross-platform compatibility\\n  - Alternatives Considered: Bash scripting (too limited), Node.js (unnecessary complexity)\\n\\n### Key Libraries\\n- `json`: Native JSON parsing\\n- `rich`: Advanced terminal formatting and color support\\n- `watchdog`: File system monitoring for real-time updates\\n- `colorama`: Cross-platform terminal color support\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Task Parser (`task_parser.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Read project tracking JSON from `~/.ensemble/projects/`\\n- Parse and validate task metadata\\n- Extract task status, progress, and details\\n\\n**Input**: Project JSON file\\n**Output**: Structured task data\\n\\n### 2. Display Formatter (`display_manager.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Convert parsed tasks to human-readable format\\n- Apply color coding and status icons\\n- Generate task summary statistics\\n\\n**Features**:\\n- Status icon mapping: \\n  - \\u2705 Completed tasks\\n  - \\u26a1 In-progress tasks\\n  - \\u23f3 Pending tasks\\n  - \\u274c Blocked tasks\\n\\n### 3. Update Watcher (`file_watcher.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Monitor project tracking file for changes\\n- Trigger task list refresh\\n- Handle file access errors gracefully\\n\\n## D. Data Flow Diagram\\n```\\n[Project JSON] \\u2192 [Task Parser] \\u2192 [Validation] \\u2192 [Display Formatter] \\u2192 [Terminal Display]\\n                      \\u2191                               \\u2193\\n               [File Watcher] \\u2190----------- [Periodic Refresh]\\n```\\n\\n## E. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\ntmux_monitoring_dashboard/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 scripts/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 monitoring/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_watcher.py        # Main script\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_parser.py          # JSON parsing logic\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 display_manager.py      # Formatting and display\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 file_watcher.py         # Real-time update mechanism\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 requirements.txt                # Python dependencies\\n```\\n\\n## F. Error Handling Strategy\\n- Graceful handling of missing/malformed project files\\n- Configurable logging for debugging\\n- Fallback display for incomplete data\\n- Retry mechanisms for file access issues\\n\\n## G. Performance Considerations\\n- Lightweight parsing (minimal CPU usage)\\n- Efficient file watching\\n- Update interval: 1-2 seconds\\n- Minimal memory footprint\\n\\n## H. Deployment Approach\\n- Callable as standalone Python script\\n- Embeddable in tmux dashboard\\n- Cross-platform compatibility (macOS, Linux)\\n\\n## I. Testing Strategy\\n1. Unit Tests\\n   - Task parsing accuracy\\n   - Display formatting\\n   - Error handling scenarios\\n\\n2. Integration Tests\\n   - File watching reliability\\n   - Real-time update performance\\n   - Tmux integration\\n\\n## J. Open Questions / User Input Needed\\n- Preferred update interval (currently 1-2 seconds)\\n- Desired level of task detail in display\\n- Custom color scheme preferences\\n\\n## K. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Risk**: Inconsistent project file format\\n   **Mitigation**: Robust schema validation, default values\\n\\n2. **Risk**: Performance overhead\\n   **Mitigation**: Efficient parsing, minimal background processing\\n\\n3. **Risk**: Cross-platform compatibility\\n   **Mitigation**: Extensive testing, use of cross-platform libraries"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Tq9CP64gpMWCjRWjeRFHUW', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'mkdir -p "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/scripts/monitoring"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Tq9CP64gpMWCjRWjeRFHUW', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01W6xPqxptqEspwTrXPurXgu', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/requirements.txt', 'content': 'rich>=13.0.0\nwatchdog>=3.0.0\ncolorama>=0.4.6'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01W6xPqxptqEspwTrXPurXgu', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/requirements.txt", "backup_path": null, "was_overwrite": false}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LJFXg8UNCdZv4nvzAXyztA', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/scripts/monitoring/task_parser.py', 'content': '"""\nTask Parser Module\n\nResponsible for reading and parsing project tracking JSON files.\nValidates task metadata and extracts structured task data.\n"""\n\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Any\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom enum import Enum\n\n\nclass TaskStatus(Enum):\n    """Enumeration of task status values"""\n    TODO = "todo"\n    IN_PROGRESS = "in_progress"\n    COMPLETED = "completed"\n    BLOCKED = "blocked"\n    CANCELLED = "cancelled"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Task:\n    """Data class representing a task"""\n    id: str\n    description: str\n    status: TaskStatus\n    assigned_to: Optional[str] = None\n    created_at: Optional[str] = None\n    updated_at: Optional[str] = None\n    notes: Optional[str] = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Project:\n    """Data class representing a project"""\n    id: str\n    name: str\n    description: str\n    created_at: str\n    tasks: List[Task]\n    notes: List[Dict[str, Any]]\n\n\nclass TaskParser:\n    """Handles parsing of project tracking JSON files"""\n\n    def __init__(self, projects_dir: Optional[str] = None):\n        """\n        Initialize task parser\n        \n        Args:\n            projects_dir: Directory containing project JSON files.\n                         Defaults to ~/.ensemble/projects/\n        """\n        if projects_dir is None:\n            home = Path.home()\n            self.projects_dir = home / ".ensemble" / "projects"\n        else:\n            self.projects_dir = Path(projects_dir)\n\n    def get_project_files(self) -> List[Path]:\n        """\n        Get list of all project JSON files\n        \n        Returns:\n            List of Path objects for project files\n        """\n        if not self.projects_dir.exists():\n            return []\n        \n        return [f for f in self.projects_dir.glob("*.json") if f.is_file()]\n\n    def parse_project_file(self, file_path: Path) -> Optional[Project]:\n        """\n        Parse a single project JSON file\n        \n        Args:\n            file_path: Path to the project JSON file\n            \n        Returns:\n            Project object if successful, None if parsing fails\n        """\n        try:\n            with open(file_path, \'r\', encoding=\'utf-8\') as f:\n                data = json.load(f)\n            \n            return self._parse_project_data(data)\n        \n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, FileNotFoundError, KeyError) as e:\n            print(f"Error parsing {file_path}: {e}")\n            return None\n\n    def _parse_project_data(self, data: Dict[str, Any]) -> Project:\n        """\n        Parse project data from dictionary\n        \n        Args:\n            data: Dictionary containing project data\n            \n        Returns:\n            Project object\n        """\n        # Parse tasks\n        tasks = []\n        for task_data in data.get("tasks", []):\n            task = self._parse_task_data(task_data)\n            if task:\n                tasks.append(task)\n\n        # Parse notes\n        notes = data.get("notes", [])\n\n        return Project(\n            id=data["id"],\n            name=data["name"],\n            description=data.get("description", ""),\n            created_at=data.get("created_at", ""),\n            tasks=tasks,\n            notes=notes\n        )\n\n    def _parse_task_data(self, task_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> Optional[Task]:\n        """\n        Parse task data from dictionary\n        \n        Args:\n            task_data: Dictionary containing task data\n            \n        Returns:\n            Task object if successful, None if parsing fails\n        """\n        try:\n            status_str = task_data.get("status", "todo")\n            \n            # Map status string to enum\n            try:\n                status = TaskStatus(status_str)\n            except ValueError:\n                status = TaskStatus.TODO  # Default fallback\n\n            return Task(\n                id=task_data["id"],\n                description=task_data["description"],\n                status=status,\n                assigned_to=task_data.get("assigned_to"),\n                created_at=task_data.get("created_at"),\n                updated_at=task_data.get("updated_at"),\n                notes=task_data.get("notes")\n            )\n        \n        except KeyError as e:\n            print(f"Missing required task field: {e}")\n            return None\n\n    def get_all_projects(self) -> List[Project]:\n        """\n        Parse all project files in the projects directory\n        \n        Returns:\n            List of Project objects\n        """\n        projects = []\n        project_files = self.get_project_files()\n        \n        for file_path in project_files:\n            project = self.parse_project_file(file_path)\n            if project:\n                projects.append(project)\n        \n        return projects\n\n    def get_all_tasks(self) -> List[Task]:\n        """\n        Get all tasks from all projects\n        \n        Returns:\n            List of Task objects from all projects\n        """\n        tasks = []\n        projects = self.get_all_projects()\n        \n        for project in projects:\n            tasks.extend(project.tasks)\n        \n        return tasks\n\n    def get_task_statistics(self) -> Dict[str, int]:\n        """\n        Get task statistics across all projects\n        \n        Returns:\n            Dictionary with task counts by status\n        """\n        tasks = self.get_all_tasks()\n        stats = {status.value: 0 for status in TaskStatus}\n        \n        for task in tasks:\n            stats[task.status.value] += 1\n        \n        return stats\n\n    def validate_projects_directory(self) -> bool:\n        """\n        Check if projects directory exists and is accessible\n        \n        Returns:\n            True if directory exists and is readable, False otherwise\n        """\n        try:\n            return self.projects_dir.exists() and self.projects_dir.is_dir()\n        except OSError:\n            return False'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LJFXg8UNCdZv4nvzAXyztA', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "ROGUE AGENT DETECTED: Agent \'\' attempted to write code file \'/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/scripts/monitoring/task_parser.py\' but lacks can_write_code permission. This agent is a supervisor/coordinator and should delegate to code writers."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a  agent.\n\n## Purpose\n\n\n## Instructions\n\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the followi