\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 51.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 11.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I executed the project workflow efficiently by quickly identifying that no implementation was required. I leveraged the Development Manager to verify the existing code meets all milestone requirements...\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'w